 cooperation that specializes in mediating between individuals belonging to an homogeneous group. It is often abbreviated as p2p. The company offers a meeting point, e.g. an online database and communication service that connects these individuals (these could include offering personal objects for rent, providing certain products or services, or the sharing of information and experiences).\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Mediate a group of individuals and organizations that have similar interests. You offer a meeting point, a way to connect all these actors, facilitating transactions among themselves (they can share things or offer eachother services).\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"performance_based_contracting\",\n      \"name\": \"Performance-based Contracting\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A product's price is not based upon the physical value, but on the performance or valuable outcome it delivers in the form of a service. Performance based contractors are often strongly integrated into the value creation process of their customers. Special expertise and economies of scale result in lower production and maintenance costs of a product, which can be forwarded to the customer. Extreme variants of this model are represented by different operation schemes in which the product remains the property of the company and operated by it.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offering a guarantee of performance, utility. This may be achieved through a material artifact (ex. you don't sell a bolb, you guarantee lighting in a building). Leads to a stronger relation with your beneficiaries.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"razor_bladerent_instead_of_buy\",\n      \"name\": \"Razor BladeRent Instead of Buy\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The basic product is cheap or given away for free. The consumable that are needed to use or operate it, on the other hamd, are expensive and sold at high margins. The initial product's price lowers customers' barrier to purchase, while the subsequent recurring sales cross-finance it. Usualy, these products are technologically bound to each other to further enhance this effect.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"A basic offering that is made very accessible, which requires other parts / modules in order to operate properly, which ensure your sustainability. It is based on repetitive interactions with your beneficiaries - repetitive game.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"use_with_caution\"\n      ],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rent_instead_of_buy\",\n      \"name\": \"Rent instead of buy\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The customer does not buy a product, but instead rents it. This lowers the capital typically needed to gain access to the product. The company itself benefits from higher profits on each product, as it is paid for the duration of the rental period. Both parties benefit from higher efficiency in product utilization as time of non-usage, which unecessarely binds capital, is reduced on each product.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Make your offering more accessible to your beneficiaries, knowing that cost of ownership may be high in some cases. Leads to higher efficiency in utilization, increase the utility of the resource as the idle time is reduced. you focus on providing the access service and on maintaining the asset.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"revenu_sharing\",\n      \"name\": \"Revenu Sharing\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Revenue sharing refers to the firm's practice of sharing revenues with tiehr stakeholders, such as complementors or even rivals. Thus, in this business model, advantagous properties are merged to create symbiotic effects in which additional profits are shared with partners participating in the extended value creation. One party is able to obtain a share of revenue from another that benefits from increased value for its customer base.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Share your benefits with your stakeholders, complementors and even with your rivals. Creates symbiotic effects. Offerings from various agents are merged, benefiting from merged advantageous properties, benefiting from the higher valuation of the agregated offer. One actor may benefit more financialy, while another one may benefit more from increased visibility and activity.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reverse_engineering\",\n      \"name\": \"Reverse Engineering\",\n      \"traditional\": \"This pattern refers to obtaining a competitor's product, taking it apart and using this information to produce a similar or compatible product. Because no huge investment in research or development is necessary, these products can be offered at a lower price than the original product.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Offer reproductions of other organizations' offerings, at lower costs, making them more accessible.  This is also the mode of production and reproduction in commons-based peer production, where development is done in the developed world by people with technical skills and time on their hands, and the models are then remixed and materialized in the developing world.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reverse_innovation\",\n      \"name\": \"Reverse Innovation\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Simple and inexpensive products that were developed within and for emerging markets are also sold in industrial countries. The term \\\"reverse\\\" refers to the process by which new products are typically developed in industrial countries and then adappted to fit the emerging market needs.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offer in the developed world is inspired from solutions developed in the developing world.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"robin_hood\",\n      \"name\": \"Robin Hood\",\n      \"traditional\": \"the same product or service is provided to the rich at a much higher price than to the poor. Thus, the main bulk of profits are generated from the wealthy customer base. Serving the poor is nt profitable per se, but creates economies of scale, which other providers cannot achieve. Additionally, it has a positive effect on the company's image.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Ask more for your offering from the rich than from the poor. Make the rich pay for the poor, help the poor and benefit from that image. Benefit from ability to penetrate poor economies.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"self_service\",\n      \"name\": \"Self-service\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A part of the value creation ois transferred to the customer in exchange for lower price of the service or product. This is particularly suited for process steps that add relatively little perceived value for the customer, but incur high costs. Customers benefit from efficiency and time savings, while putting in their own effort. This can also increase efficiency, since in some cases, the customer can execute a calue adding step more quickly and in a more target-oriented manner than the company.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Transfer some processes that can generate high costs to you, to your beneficiaries (ex. assembly when you send them a kit). These transfered processes must not increase the valuation of your offer much. This increases efficiency, since the user can perform this process acording to his needs.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shop_in_shop\",\n      \"name\": \"Shop in Shop\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Instead of opening new branches, a partner is chosen whos branches can profit from integrating the company's offerings in a way that initiated a small shop within another shop (a win-win situation). The hosting store can benefit from more attracted customers and is able to gain constant revenue from the hosted shop in the form of rent. The hosted company gains access to cheaper resources such as space, location or workforce.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Share space, physical or digital, with another organization, benefit from a larger offer, mutualizing resources and processes, location, as well as from a larger flow of potential beneficiaries.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"Ex. a fablab in a library.\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution_provider\",\n      \"name\": \"Solution Provider\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A full service provider offers total coverage of products and services in a particular domain, consolidated via a single point of contact. Special know-how is given to the customer in order to increase his or her efficiency and performance. By becoming a full service provider, a company can prevent revenue losses by extending their service and adding it to the product. Additionally, close contact with the customer allows great insight into the customer habits and needs, which can be used to improve the products and services.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offer covers everything in a specific domain, consolidated via a single point of entry. You provide special know-how, in order to increase efficiancy and performance. This model helps to prevent losses, extends your offerings. Also benefit from close relation with your beneficiaries, greater insight into their needs, which can be used as feedback.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subscription\",\n      \"name\": \"Subscription\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The customer pays a regular fee, typically on a monthly or anual basis, in order to gain access to a product or service. While customers mostly benefit from lower usage cost and general service availability, the company generates a more steady income stream.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your beneficiaries reciprocate on a regular basis for a basic or generic offer. Makes your offer more affordable, lower usage costs and higher offer availability. Your operations become more predictable, steady.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"supermarket\",\n      \"name\": \"Supermarket\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The company sells a large variety of readily available products and accessories under one roof. Generally, the assortment of products is large but the prices are kept low. More customers are attracted due to the great range of offers, while economies of scale yield advantages for the company.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"A great variety of offers that are widely needed. Benefit from the scale of the operation.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"target_the_poor\",\n      \"name\": \"Target the Poor\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The product or service offering does not target the premium customer, but rather the customer positioned at the base of the pyramid. Customers with lower purchasing power benefit from affordable products. The company generates small profits with each product sold, but benefits from the higher sales numbers that usually some with the scale of the customer base.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offering benefits the poor. Your focus is on increasing the number of beneficiaries, cater to the needs of the poor.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"trash_to_cash\",\n      \"name\": \"Trash to Cash\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Used products are collected and either sold in other parts of the world of transformed into new products. The profit scheme is essentially based on low-to-no purchase price. Resource costs for the company are practically eliminated, whilst the supplier's waste disposal is either provided, or associated costs are reduced. This also addresses customers' potential environmental awarness ideals.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Recycling, curcular economy. Your ofering is transforming, upscaling.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"two_sided_market\",\n      \"name\": \"Two-sided Market\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A two-sided market facilitates interactions between multiple interdependent groups of customers. The value of the platrform increases as more groups or as more individual members of each group are using it. The two sides usually come from disparate groups, e.g. business and private interest groups.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offer is to facilitate interactions between multiple interdependent groups of customers. The offer becomes more valuable as more groups or as more individual members of each group are participating. The two sides usually come from disparate groups, interested in transacting with each other.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ultimate_luxury\",\n      \"name\": \"Ultimate Luxury\",\n      \"traditional\": \"This pattern describes the strategy of a company to focus on the upper side of society's pyramid. This allows a company to distinguish its products or services greatly from others. High standards of quality or exclusive privileges are the main focus to attract these kinks of customer